  "full_text": "I think it's given us a really critical insight into how the brain actually produces these very basic functions. So those who can't see, those who can't hear, if you can start to map out those areas of the brain which are involved in those processes, that will help in kind of recreating ways for them to facilitate their hearing and their vision. And they use no ionizing radiation like x-rays or CT scans do. No studies have linked MRIs to any adverse health effects. So I'm not too worried about my noggin after all these photos. I think it looks pretty good, thanks to physics. And thanks to you for watching this video, and I hope you learned something. And if you want to keep on learning physics, hit subscribe. Close to 300 280 Go to Wix.com to create your stunning website today. Choose from hundreds of templates. Drag and drop.",
